---
import HsmMapLegend from './HsmMapLegend.astro';
---

<figure class="hsm-figure hsm-figure--wide">
  <div class="hsm-figure__chrome">
    <p class="hsm-figure__eyebrow">FIG. 01</p>
    <p class="hsm-figure__title">Records are not habitat</p>
    <p class="hsm-figure__lede">
      Bat records cluster where people have looked. A suitability model gives us a different picture of the landscape.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="hsm-figure__frame hsm-compare">
    <div class="hsm-compare__panel">
      <p class="hsm-compare__label">Recording intensity</p>
      <p class="hsm-compare__meta">All bat species · grouped into 1 km squares</p>
      <img
        src="/images/hsm/panel-recording-intensity.png"
        alt="Yorkshire map of aggregated bat recording intensity, with higher values concentrated in the south and west."
        width="960"
        height="840"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <HsmMapLegend kind="intensity" />
    </div>
    <div class="hsm-compare__panel">
      <p class="hsm-compare__label">Predicted suitability</p>
      <p class="hsm-compare__meta">Daubenton’s bat · in flight</p>
      <img
        src="/images/hsm/panel-daubenton-if.png"
        alt="Yorkshire map of predicted Daubenton’s bat in-flight suitability, with higher values along waterways and valleys."
        width="960"
        height="840"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <HsmMapLegend kind="suitability" />
    </div>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="hsm-figure__caption">
    Left: recording intensity across all bat species, used as a rough indication of survey effort.
    Right: predicted habitat suitability for Daubenton’s bat in flight. Neither map shows where this species is definitely present or absent.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .hsm-figure {
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }

  .hsm-figure--wide {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: none;
    margin-left: 0;
  }

  .hsm-figure__chrome {
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
  }

  .hsm-figure__eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 0.2rem;
    color: var(--colour-rust);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  }

  .hsm-figure__title {
    margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }

  .hsm-figure__lede {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--colour-muted);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    max-width: 42rem;
  }

  .hsm-figure__frame {
    border: 1px solid var(--colour-rule);
    background: #f7f4ec;
    padding: 0.85rem;
  }

  .hsm-compare {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 0.9rem;
  }

  .hsm-compare__panel {
    min-width: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.35rem;
  }

  .hsm-compare__label {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .hsm-compare__meta {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--colour-muted);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
  }

  .hsm-compare__panel img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--colour-rule);
    background: #f7f4ec;
  }

  .hsm-figure__caption {
    margin-top: 0.65rem;
    color: var(--colour-muted);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    max-width: 48rem;
  }

  .hsm-figure__caption code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78em;
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .hsm-compare {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
